### Statistical Tests & Data Science Methods

1. **Data Processing:** Deal with problems of missing data and date and time information and data corruption․ Make seasonal samples of our data․

2. **Hypothesis Testing:** Conduct a permutation test to evaluate the statistical significance of differences in average pollutant concentrations by season․ A permutation test can show whether differences in average concentrations by season are statistically meaningful․

3. **Bootstrap Intervals:** Compute bootstrap confidence intervals for seasonal differences in average pollutant levels to evaluate the precision of estimates of pollutant levels․

4. **Data Analasys & Visualization:** Make scatter and line plots by time and heat maps to identify weather and seasonal trends related to air pollution․







